+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+While system and cruise are active, release after about 0.4s or longer on the accelerator selects the dashboard speed if it exceeds the pre-press setting. Accelerating from a 70 setting to 100 and releasing at 85 selects 85, without saving the pedal peak.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Enable this setting and use it during existing cruise operation. Short gas-tap actions remain. Brake, CANCEL, buttons, speed commands, invalid input or loss of cruise revoke that cycle; press again after recovery.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Existing setting bounds, vehicle-owned PCM speed modes and automatic speed, lead, curve and navigation control remain in effect. Porter uses existing button requests, so actual stock-setting changes depend on vehicle acceptance and may be delayed. Separate from automatic SET in standby.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
